'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-vo-j-005r-streamer-capture-ceiling-and-skew.spin2
''   Purpose....  VO-J-005 REDUCED: the two source-silent facts about the
''                streamer's pins-to-WRFAST digital capture - (E) the
''                sustained capture rate, by an NCO ladder 1:16 .. 1:1 in the
''                4-, 8- and 16-pin modes, and (S) whether a %FFF filter
''                selection delays a lane against an unfiltered lane
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-J-005, reduced; close-out study step 8)

  This rig replaces the full VO-J-005 rig for the bench run
  (campaigns/2026-08-manual-corrections/tests/test-vo-j-005-streamer-pin-
  capture.spin2, 699 lines, accepted and unchanged).  The recheck
  (bench-groupD-recheck.md section 6) killed arms A-D as QUESTIONS (the
  capture path is documented: silicon-doc-text.txt:1535, Parallax's worked
  capture of a smart-pin TX through an adjacent pin at spin2-v55-text.txt
  :1144; the IN rule at SD:3706 / SD:3767; arm B, base 12 vs 8, by SD:1443-
  1454 and EF-059/064/065).  They run here ONLY AS GATES, and the run is aimed
  at the two facts deliverables/ai/P2/architecture/streamer/pin-capture.yaml
  :296-304 records as "NOT STATED ... never measured":

  E  SUSTAINED CAPTURE RATE.  The NCO can roll over every clock (SD:1288-1296)
     and the FIFO is described as moving "any combination of bytes, words, or
     longs, at any rate, up to one long per clock" (SD:3003); no source states
     a sustained CAPTURE rate, and nothing has been measured.  ("Sustained" here
     means 1024 consecutive samples per capture = 512 / 1024 / 2048 bytes in the
     4- / 8- / 16-pin mode: a limit that shows only on a long run, not a one-off
     burst.  The FIFO depth is not stated in the silicon-doc text, so no figure
     is claimed for how far past it the run goes.)  A stimulus that
     toggles every 64 clocks (smart-pin TRANSITION mode, exact) is captured at
     NCO 1:16, 1:8, 1:4, 1:2, 1:1 in three modes: 4 pins (WFBYTE, 0.5 byte per
     sample), 8 pins (WFBYTE, 1 byte per sample) and 16 pins (WFWORD, 2 bytes
     per sample).  At 1:N the recovered distance between consecutive edges
     must be EXACTLY 64/N samples; a dropped sample shortens it, a stalled
     streamer stretches it, a streamer that never finishes sets LATE.  The
     fastest rung that is exact (with every slower rung exact) IS the measured
     sustained ceiling of that mode.  NO CEILING IS PREDICTED.
  S  FILTER SKEW.  Whether a %FFF = 100 (filt0) selection on a monitor pin
     delays its lane against an unfiltered monitor of the same signal, and by
     how many clocks.  SD Table 30 (:2808-2847) gives each filter a "low-pass
     time" (clocks per sample x flip-flops; filt0 = 1 x 2); that is a time
     constant, NOT a stated edge delay.  NO SKEW IS PREDICTED.  Measured at
     1 sample per clock (1 clock resolution), rising and falling edges
     separately, with a control (two UNFILTERED monitors: the lane-to-lane
     skew of the capture path itself), with an ENGAGEMENT leg and with filt0
     set to 2, 3, 5 and 8 flip-flops at tap 0 (HUBSET, SD:2784; restored to
     the default at the end).  Tap 0 gives at most 8 clocks of delay, which a
     capture path that ignored the filter could not be told apart from "no
     delay"; so first the ENGAGEMENT leg sets filt0 to 5 flip-flops at tap 3
     (HUBSET ##$4000_0043 = FILT0_BASE + 2 << 5 + 3, SD:2784 / SD:2605: length
     field %10 = 5 flip-flops SD:2790, tap 3 = every 8th clock SD:2792) whose
     low-pass time is 5 x 8 = 40 clocks.  If the captured lane is the filtered
     pin state, MON_F lags MON_R by about 32..42 clocks on every edge (the
     phase of the tap against the edge is not controlled).  The leg is
     ENGAGED when every compared edge of every repetition lags by 16..63
     clocks; otherwise every S reading prints "filter not observed to engage;
     NO DELAY is void" and no NO DELAY verdict is possible.  Whether the
     streamer's captured lane IS the filtered state is itself unstated here:
     this leg decides it.

  32-pin capture is NOT run: it reads 32 pins, more than the free set
  (P0-P7, P32-P47) holds.  So the hub-limited rung (one long per clock) is
  reachable here only through the 16-pin WFWORD mode (half a long per clock).
  If no rung of any mode fails, the finding is "no ceiling at or below 16 bits
  per clock"; the 32-bit rate stays open.

RE-PIN  (the full rig used P8..P15, which are NOT free pins)
  Base P32.  The 4-pin, 8-pin and 16-pin modes at pin group %ppp = %100
  ("select pins 63..32", SD:1449) are expected to read P32..P35, P32..P39
  and P32..P47: all inside the free set.  That the narrower modes take the
  LOWEST pins of the group is an inference (SD:1549 says it for the ADC
  modes: "the lower 8 or 16 pins of the 32 pins selected by the %ppp bits";
  SD:1454 resolves sub-8-pin bases with D[19:17]); gate A is the check - it
  drives P32 and P35 and requires lane N = pin P(32+N) in every mode, so a
  group that read other pins would fail A, not pass silently.
  4-pin: D[22:20] = %100 selects the group, D[19] = pin bit 2 = 0 -> base P32
  (base << 17 = $0040_0000).  Re-derived from the layout table (SD:1370-1384):
    4 pins   1110 dddd wppp p00a   X_4P_4DAC1_WFBYTE   %1110_DDDD_WPPP_P00A
    8 pins   1110 dddd wppp 1110   X_8P_1DAC8_WFBYTE   %1110_DDDD_WPPP_1110
    16 pins  1111 dddd wppp 0000   X_16P_2DAC8_WFWORD  %1111_DDDD_WPPP_0000
  (spin2-v55-text.txt:1608-1613 gives the symbol names and templates).  Words
  composed with | (never +): symbol | X_WRITE_ON | (32 << 17) | SAMPLES.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  NOTHING attached.  Pins touched: P32..P47 only.
    P32 BUS    smart pin TRANSITION | P_OE, X = 64 clocks per transition; its
               own IN is the completion flag
    P33 MON_R  smart pin mode off, A = relative -1 (P32): the UNFILTERED
               monitor of the BUS pin's level
    P34 MON_F  smart pin mode off, A = relative -2 (P32), with %FFF = 100
               (filt0): the FILTERED monitor (the skew legs; in the ladder it
               is just a second lane); in the skew control leg it is
               UNFILTERED
    P35 NULL   plain pin driven low; rides in every capture and MUST read 0
    P36..P47   held at a 15 k-ohm LOW (smart pin mode off, DIR high) so the
               wider modes read a defined 0 on every lane they do not use
  Before anything is driven hard P32..P47 are held at the 15 k-ohm LOW and
  read back: a pin that reads 1 has something attached, and the run STOPS
  naming it.
  Cog 0 (Spin2, the only cog with the debugger, DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001)
  starts ONE Spin2 cog that owns the streamer and every pin; it measures and
  reports nothing.  Cog 0 waits for it (30 s timeout), then analyses nothing
  itself - it only prints the worker's records.  No debug() runs in the
  measuring cog (EF-057: with -d the highest-priority interrupt is the
  debugger's; DEBUG_COGS keeps it out of the streamer's cog).

GATES  (a failure prints RIG FAIL and the dependent result is withheld)
  CERT  P32..P47 read 0 under the weak low  (else STOP: pins busy)
  CFG   the configuration and streamer command words equal the values decoded
        below (compile-time symbols against typed constants)
  A     per mode: six static captures (patterns, bit 0 = P32: %0000, %0001,
        %1000, %0010, %0100, %0110) return EVERY sample equal to the driven
        pattern, EXACTLY the expected number of bytes written (an over-run is
        a failure too) and no sentinel byte left: the path writes,
        discriminates, and lane N = pin P(32+N) for every lane 0..3
  PAD   16 longs after the capture buffer are filled with $A5A5_A5A5 before
        every capture and checked after it: any other value is an over-run of
        the buffer by the streamer (RIG FAIL).  (The fill is not zero because
        a zero over-run would be invisible in a quiet pattern.)
  O     4-pin nibble order: the 1:16 capture is analysed with the low nibble
        first (SD:1456 "bits bottom-first") AND with the high nibble first.
        The order is decided ONLY when exactly one of the two analyses is
        exact: if both are exact the capture cannot tell the orders apart
        (the edges sit on the byte boundary), so the capture is repeated up
        to 8 times, delaying the burst start by one 1:16 sample (16 clocks)
        per try so the edge parity against the byte changes.  If no try
        disagrees: "nibble order undetermined" and the gate FAILS (the 4-pin
        mode is VOID: no ladder, no skew verdict); neither exact in every
        try -> also VOID
  C     (no streamer) over 20 ms the cog sees P33 CHANGE at least 20 times
        (the stimulus runs); P32's own IN changes are counted and printed
  D     one 4-pin 1:1 capture: the NULL lane (P35) is all zero and the MON_R
        lane carries the waveform (>= 8 edges).  The BUS lane (P32) edge
        count is printed: <= 1 is the documented IN rule (a lane with one
        edge is a LIVE lane carrying the flag), >= 8 would refute it
  E0    the 1:16 rung of each mode is EXACT in all repetitions (else that
        mode has no ceiling reading: VOID)
  S0    the unfiltered MON_R lane of every skew capture has every edge
        interval = 64 samples (the 1:1 carrier is exact) else the skew of
        that capture is void
  ENG   (not a RIG FAIL: a reading) the ENGAGEMENT leg: every compared edge of
        every repetition lags 16..63 clocks -> "ENGAGED"; anything else ->
        "filter not observed to engage": every S reading then prints "filter
        not observed to engage; NO DELAY is void" and no NO DELAY verdict
        is issued (a 0 skew then says the captured lane ignores the filter, or
        nothing about the filter - not that the filter has no delay)
  The raw values of every capture are printed whether or not a gate passed.

PRE-REGISTERED READINGS  (printed before the run; none predicted)
  E, per mode:
    NO CEILING REACHED  every rung 1:16 .. 1:1 EXACT: the mode sustains one
                        sample per clock with this stimulus
    CEILING 1:N         the fastest rung that is exact with all slower rungs
                        exact; the first failing rung's raw record is the
                        failure mode (fewer bytes, shortened/stretched
                        intervals, LATE)
    NON-MONOTONE        a faster rung is exact above a failing one
  S engagement (filt0 = 5 flip-flops, tap 3, about 40 clocks expected):
    ENGAGED         every compared edge lags 16..63 clocks
    NOT OBSERVED    anything else: "filter not observed to engage"
  S, per filter setting (rise and fall separately, over >= 3 repetitions;
  valid as a NO DELAY verdict ONLY when the engagement leg read ENGAGED):
    NO DELAY        skew = 0 clocks on both edges
    EQUALS N-FF     skew = the number of flip-flops (2, 3, 5, 8)
    EQUALS N-FF - 1 skew = flip-flops - 1
    OTHER           any other constant, or varying: the numbers are the finding
  The control leg (two unfiltered monitors) MUST read 0 on both edges; a
  non-zero control means the capture path itself skews lanes and the filter
  skew is not separable.

DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF
  The brief asks for the old rig with arms A-D only as gates and arm E plus the
  filter skew; the 8- and 16-pin ladders, the nibble-order gate, the
  unfiltered-pair skew control, the engagement leg and the filter-length legs
  are added (a ceiling
  that only the 4-pin mode could show at 0.5 byte per clock would answer
  little).  Arm B (base 12 vs 8) is dropped (killed by sources, F-361 closes
  on them; the new base needs no alternate-base check because arm A's P32-high
  and P35-high captures discriminate the lane mapping of the new base).  The
  measuring cog is a launched Spin2 cog rather than cog 0 (reporting from a
  non-measuring cog, EF-057).  The IN-contrast arms C and D print their
  documented-rule outcome but gate only on "the stimulus runs".

DEBUGGER
  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub strings and numbers and
  sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in ln_out(); the only other
  record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The listing reports the record count
  and the DEBUG data size (recorded below).

OPCODES, WORDS AND ADDRESSES  (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8, read from the .lst)
  Symbol values read from the .lst symbol table (the program also compares
  each symbol composition with the decoded value below at run time, gate CFG):
    CFG_BUS      $0000_004A   P_TRANSITION | P_OE: TT = %01 (bits 7:6, P_OE),
                              SSSSS = %00101 (bits 5:1, transition), O = 0
    CFG_MONR     $7000_0000   AAAA = %0111 (bits 31:28) = relative -1 for A;
                              mode off (SSSSS = 0), FFF = %000
    CFG_MONF     $6080_0000   AAAA = %0110 = relative -2 for A; FFF = %100
                              (bits 23:21) = A, B filtered with filt0
    CFG_MONF_NF  $6000_0000   the control: relative -2, FFF = %000
    CAP_4P       $E0C0_0400   X_4P_4DAC1_WFBYTE $E000_0000 | X_WRITE_ON
                              $0080_0000 | (32 << 17) $0040_0000 | 1024
    CAP_8P       $E0CE_0400   X_8P_1DAC8_WFBYTE $E00E_0000 | ...
    CAP_16P      $F0C0_0400   X_16P_2DAC8_WFWORD $F000_0000 | ...
    FILT0_BASE   $4000_0000   HUBSET: + length << 5 + tap (SD:2784); length
                              0..3 = 2, 3, 5, 8 flip-flops (SD:2790)
    FILT0_ENG    $4000_0043   the engagement leg: FILT0_BASE + (2 << 5) + 3
                              = length %10 (5 flip-flops), tap 3 (every 8th
                              clock, SD:2792); 5 x 8 = 40 clocks; layout
                              %0100_..._RRLL_TTTTT, SD:2605 (R = filter 0 here)
    NCO_1_16 .. NCO_1_1  $0800_0000 $1000_0000 $2000_0000 $4000_0000
                              $8000_0000 (SD:1294-1303)
    Constants: NPAT 6, PAD_LONGS 16, PAD_FILL $A5A5_A5A5, NIB_TRIES 8,
    NIB_SHIFT 16, ENG_MIN 16, ENG_MAX 63.
  The inline PASM of method capture (hub-image bytes read from the .lst, as
  little-endian longs; the local registers are method locals, so they move
  with the parameter list): SETXFRQ xfrq $FD63_C21D (opcode ...000011101) ;
  WRFAST #0,addr $FC88_01E7 ; GETCT t0 $FD63_D21A ; XINIT cmd,#0 $FCA7_CC00 ;
  TJZ shiftClk,#.noshiftClk $FB97_C601 (EEEE 1011100 10I, SD:5159; I = 1, S =
  +1 instruction: skips the WAITX when shiftClk = 0) ; WAITX shiftClk
  $FD63_C61F (EEEE 1101011 CZL DDDDDDDDD 000011111, SD:5262) ; WYPIN
  ycnt,#32 $FC27_C420 (S = #BUS = 32) ; POLLXFI WC $FD70_1624 (EEEE 1101011
  CZ0 000001011 000100100, silicon-doc-text.txt:5280) ; XSTOP = XINIT #0,#0
  $FCAC_0000 (SD:1405).  The 4-pin base: D[22:20] = %100, D[19] = 0, i.e.
  base << 17 = $0040_0000, the only change from the full rig's (8 << 17).
  The listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.
  If you edit this file, recompile with -l and re-read every row above.

HOW TO RUN
  USB serial must be connected (DEBUG rides P62/P63).  P32..P47 must be
  COMPLETELY FREE: nothing attached to any of them (the program drives P32
  hard and holds P36..P47 low through 15 kOhm; CERT reads P32..P47 under the
  weak low first and STOPS the run, naming the pins, if any reads 1).
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut
  Ctrl-F10); nothing is written to flash.
  SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT - it is the only record.
  Expected run time: the measuring cog makes about 110 captures, each
  dominated by the 1 ms settle waits of its set-up: an estimate of roughly 1
  to 5 s (not timed on silicon).  Cog 0 gives the measuring cog 30 s,
  counted in whole seconds.  A run
  that prints no "=== END" line and no DEBUG_END_SESSION within 45 s is a
  hang or a lost session: report it as such, not as a reading.
  Clock: _clkfreq = 200 MHz assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal (the listing's
  CLKMODE is $010009FB, read from the .lst); the stimulus period (64 clocks),
  the capture rates and the 30 s timeout all depend on it.
  The 32-pin rung is not run (open: it reads more pins than the free set).
  Output: the header and readings, the gate lines, one line per mode and rung,
  the ceiling lines, one line per filter leg, the engagement and skew lines,
  the PAD line, the END line, then DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000         ' system clock: 200 MHz
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  BUS             = 32                  ' smart pin: TRANSITION output
  MON_R           = BUS + 1             ' A from relative -1: unfiltered monitor
  MON_F           = BUS + 2             ' A from relative -2: filtered monitor
  NULLPIN         = BUS + 3             ' plain pin, low: rides in the capture
  LANE_BUS        = 0                   ' lane = pin - BUS
  LANE_MONR       = 1
  LANE_MONF       = 2
  LANE_NULL       = 3
  GUARD_LO        = 32                  ' pins this program touches: P32..P47
  GUARD_N         = 16
  WEAK_LO         = 36                  ' held at 15k low so unused lanes read 0
  WEAK_N          = 12

  SAMPLES         = 1024                ' NCO rollovers per capture
  BUF_LONGS       = 512                 ' 2048 bytes: the 16-pin mode's 1024 words
  BUF_BYTES       = BUF_LONGS * 4
  SENTINEL        = $A5                 ' not producible: lanes beyond 0..2 read 0

  FAST_PER        = 64                  ' clocks per transition (ladder and skew)
  SLOW_PER        = 60_000              ' 300 us per half-cycle (arm C)
  BURST_E         = 600                 ' 600 * 64 clocks: outlasts the 1:16 window (16,384)
  BURST_D         = 10                  ' 10 transitions: ends inside the 1:1 window
  BURST_C         = 40                  ' 40 * 300 us = 12 ms of the 20 ms arm C window
  C_SAMPLES       = 400
  C_INTERVAL      = 50                  ' us between arm C reads
  CAP_BUDGET      = 2_000_000           ' 10 ms: no capture may wait longer for XFI
  MIN_EDGES       = 8
  EDGE_MAX        = 16

  NPAT            = 6                   ' gate A static patterns per mode
  PAD_LONGS       = 16                  ' guard longs after bufl
  PAD_FILL        = $A5A5_A5A5          ' their fill (not producible by a capture, not zero)
  NIB_TRIES       = 8                   ' gate O: 1:16 captures, each started one sample later
  NIB_SHIFT       = 16                  ' clocks of start delay per try = one sample at 1:16
  ENG_MIN         = 16                  ' engagement leg: every skew must be >= this many clocks ...
  ENG_MAX         = 63                  ' ... and < the 64-clock edge spacing

  REPS            = 4                   ' repetitions of every ladder rung
  SREPS           = 3                   ' repetitions of every skew leg
  WORKER_SEC      = 30                 ' cog 0 waits this long for the worker (counted in whole seconds, so no clkfreq product wraps)
  WORKER_STACK    = 200
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE

  LINE_MAX        = 480
  DEC_TOP         = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS      = 10
  DEC_BASE        = 10
  HEX_DIGITS      = 8
  HEX_BITS        = 4
  HEX_GROUP       = 4
  HEX_LETTERS     = 10

CON ' ---- Configuration Words (decoded field by field) ----
  ' WRPIN word:  %AAAA_BBBB_FFF_MMMMMMMMMMMMM_TT_SSSSS_O   (SD:3750-3769)
  CFG_BUS         = P_TRANSITION | P_OE                   ' TT = %01 (P_OE), SSSSS = %00101 (transition)
  CFG_MONR        = P_MINUS1_A                            ' AAAA = %0111: A = relative -1; mode off
  CFG_MONF        = P_MINUS2_A | P_FILT0_AB               ' AAAA = %0110: A = relative -2; FFF = %100: filt0
  CFG_MONF_NF     = P_MINUS2_A                            ' the control: A = relative -2, FFF = %000 (no filter)
  CFG_BUS_X       = $0000_004A                            ' %01_00101_0 = $4A
  CFG_MONR_X      = $7000_0000
  CFG_MONF_X      = $6080_0000                            ' $6000_0000 | %100 << 21
  CFG_MONF_NF_X   = $6000_0000
  FILT0_BASE      = $4000_0000                            ' HUBSET: set filt0 = $4000_0000 + length << 5 + tap (SD:2784)
  FILT0_ENG       = FILT0_BASE + (2 << 5) + 3             ' engagement leg: length %10 = 5 flip-flops, tap 3 = every 8th clock
  FILT0_ENG_X     = $4000_0043                            ' $4000_0000 + $40 + 3

  ' Streamer command words:  symbol | X_WRITE_ON | (32 << 17) | SAMPLES
  CAP_4P          = X_4P_4DAC1_WFBYTE | X_WRITE_ON | (BUS << 17) | SAMPLES
  CAP_8P          = X_8P_1DAC8_WFBYTE | X_WRITE_ON | (BUS << 17) | SAMPLES
  CAP_16P         = X_16P_2DAC8_WFWORD | X_WRITE_ON | (BUS << 17) | SAMPLES
  CAP_4P_X        = $E0C0_0400                            ' %1110_0000_1100_0000_0000_0100_0000_0000
  CAP_8P_X        = $E0CE_0400                            ' %1110_0000_1100_1110_...
  CAP_16P_X       = $F0C0_0400                            ' %1111_0000_1100_0000_...

  ' NCO frequencies: frequency = $8000_0000 * (sample_rate / clkfreq)   (SD:1294-1303)
  NCO_1_16        = $0800_0000
  NCO_1_8         = $1000_0000
  NCO_1_4         = $2000_0000
  NCO_1_2         = $4000_0000
  NCO_1_1         = $8000_0000

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' capture modes
  #0, MD_4P, MD_8P, MD_16P
  NMODE           = MD_16P + 1
  ' ladder rungs, slowest first
  #0, RG_1_16, RG_1_8, RG_1_4, RG_1_2, RG_1_1
  NRATE           = RG_1_1 + 1
  ' skew legs: the unfiltered-pair control, the ENGAGEMENT leg (5 flip-flops, tap 3),
  ' then filt0 with 2, 3, 5, 8 flip-flops at tap 0
  #0, SK_CTL, SK_ENG, SK_FF2, SK_FF3, SK_FF5, SK_FF8
  NFILT           = SK_FF8 + 1
  ' phases of the worker (progress, for a STALLED line)
  #0, PH_NONE, PH_CERT, PH_A, PH_O, PH_C, PH_D, PH_E, PH_S, PH_END
  ' arm A record longs
  #0, AF_WROTE, AF_BAD, AF_FIRST
  AW              = 3
  ' ladder record longs
  #0, EF_WROTE, EF_LATE, EF_EDGES, EF_FIRST, EF_LAST, EF_MIN, EF_MAX, EF_BAD, EF_NULL, EF_EXACT
  EW              = 10
  ' arm D record longs: wrote, late, then per lane edges, highs, first (lanes 0..3)
  DW              = 14
  ' skew record longs
  #0, SF_WROTE, SF_LATE, SF_BAD, SF_NULL, SF_NA, SF_NB, SF_DIRMIS, SF_RMIN, SF_RMAX, SF_FMIN, SF_FMAX, SF_NR, SF_NF
  SW              = 13

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long bufl[BUF_LONGS]                  ' the capture buffer, long-aligned
  long bufPad[PAD_LONGS]                ' guard: PAD_FILL before and after every capture (an over-run changes it)
  ' ---- worker -> reporter ----
  long wPhase, wDetail, wDone
  long wStack[WORKER_STACK]
  long certMask                         ' bit n = P(32+n) read 1 under the weak low
  long modeOk[NMODE]
  long nibHi                            ' 4-pin: 1 = high nibble first
  long nibState                         ' 0 low first exact, 1 high first exact, 2 neither exact, 3 undetermined
  long nibTries, nibBoth, nibNeither    ' gate O: captures made, tries where both / neither order was exact
  long padHits, capCount                ' captures whose pad changed, captures made
  long aRec[NMODE * NPAT * AW]
  long cBus, cMon
  long dRec[DW]
  long eRec[NMODE * NRATE * REPS * EW]
  long sRec[NFILT * SREPS * SW]
  long sEdgeA[NFILT * EDGE_MAX], sEdgeB[NFILT * EDGE_MAX]   ' repetition 0's edges
  long sEdgeNA[NFILT], sEdgeNB[NFILT]
  ' ---- analysis scratch (worker) ----
  long anEdges, anFirst, anLast, anMin, anMax, anBad, anNull
  long tmpA[EDGE_MAX], tmpB[EDGE_MAX]
  ' ---- reporter ----
  long failCnt
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | workCog, startCt, secCnt
'' Start the measuring cog, wait for it, print its records.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local workCog - cog the measuring cog started in
' @local startCt - CT at the start of the current second of the wait
' @local secCnt - whole seconds waited so far

  linePos := 0
  failCnt := 0
  print_header()
  check_words()
  longfill(@aRec, UNWRITTEN, NMODE * NPAT * AW)
  longfill(@bufPad, PAD_FILL, PAD_LONGS)
  padHits := 0
  capCount := 0
  nibTries := 0
  nibBoth := 0
  nibNeither := 0
  longfill(@dRec, UNWRITTEN, DW)
  longfill(@eRec, UNWRITTEN, NMODE * NRATE * REPS * EW)
  longfill(@sRec, UNWRITTEN, NFILT * SREPS * SW)
  longfill(@sEdgeNA, 0, NFILT)
  longfill(@sEdgeNB, 0, NFILT)
  longfill(@modeOk, 0, NMODE)
  wPhase := PH_NONE
  wDetail := 0
  wDone := 0
  certMask := 0
  nibState := 2
  nibHi := 0
  cBus := UNWRITTEN
  cMon := UNWRITTEN
  workCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, worker(), @wStack)
  if workCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: cogspin expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(workCog)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no measuring cog) - NO VERDICT ==="))
    finish()
  startCt := getct()
  secCnt := 0
  repeat until wDone == DONE_V
    ' whole seconds are counted one at a time: clkfreq * N wraps in 32-bit
    ' arithmetic for N > 10 at 200 MHz
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      startCt += clkfreq
      secCnt++
    if secCnt >= WORKER_SEC
      cogstop(workCog)
      pinclear(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)
      hubset(FILT0_BASE)                ' the measuring cog may have left filt0 changed
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: STALLED - the measuring cog did not finish within "))
      ln_d(WORKER_SEC)
      ln_s(string(" s; it stopped in phase "))
      ln_d(wPhase)
      ln_s(string(" detail "))
      ln_d(wDetail)
      ln_s(string(" (1 CERT, 2 A, 3 O, 4 C, 5 D, 6 E, 7 S); pins cleared by cog 0; the records written so far are reported"))
      ln_out()
      failCnt++
      quit
  ln_s(string("=== measuring cog "))
  ln_d(workCog)
  say(string(" ==="))
  report_all()
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output.
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_d(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as signed

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_cnt(countVal, ofVal)
' Append "n of m".
'
' @param countVal - the count
' @param ofVal - the total

  ln_d(countVal)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(ofVal)

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI rig_fail(pStr)
' Count one RIG FAIL and start its line; the caller appends the details and
' sends the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the text

  failCnt++
  ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
  ln_s(pStr)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' header and word check (cog 0)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header()
' Print the rig identity and the pre-registered readings, before any run.
'

  say(string("=== VO-J-005r: streamer pin-capture - sustained ceiling (NCO ladder) and %FFF filter skew (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz, nothing attached) ==="))
  say(string("Pins P32..P47 only: BUS P32 (TRANSITION, 64 clocks/transition) | MON_R P33 (A = rel -1, unfiltered) | MON_F P34 (A = rel -2, filt0 in the skew legs) | NULL P35 (low) | P36..P47 held at 15k low. Base P32 = pin group %100."))
  say(string("Measured, not predicted: no source states a sustained capture rate or a filter lane delay (pin-capture.yaml 'NOT STATED'). Gates CERT, CFG, A, O, C, D, E0, S0 withhold dependent results, never the raw values."))
  say(string("E: 4-, 8-, 16-pin captures of an exact 64-clock stimulus at NCO 1:16 .. 1:1, 1024 samples, 4 reps each. Rung EXACT = every edge interval = 64/N samples, all bytes written, no LATE, NULL lane silent."))
  say(string("E readings per mode: NO CEILING REACHED | CEILING 1:N (fastest exact rung, all slower exact) | NON-MONOTONE. 32-pin capture is not run (reads more than the free pins)."))
  say(string("S: edge position of MON_F minus MON_R at 1 sample/clock; control = both unfiltered (MUST be 0); ENGAGEMENT leg filt0 = 5 flip-flops tap 3 (about 40 clocks); then filt0 = 2, 3, 5, 8 flip-flops at tap 0."))
  say(string("S readings: NO DELAY | EQUALS N-FF | EQUALS N-FF - 1 | OTHER. ENGAGEMENT: ENGAGED = every compared edge lags 16..63 clocks, else 'filter not observed to engage' and NO DELAY is void for every leg."))
  say(string("Gate A: six patterns per mode (%0000 %0001 %1000 %0010 %0100 %0110). Gate PAD: 16 guard longs after the buffer. Gate O: low-first and high-first must DISAGREE in one of up to 8 captures, else 'nibble order undetermined'."))
  say(string("Run needs USB serial (DEBUG on P62/P63); save the whole console output; P32..P47 must be completely free; no '=== END' within 45 s = hang / lost session. The 32-pin rung is not run (open)."))

PRI check_words()
' Compare each symbol-composed word with the value decoded in the header;
' a mismatch is a RIG FAIL (the CFG gate).
'

  if CFG_BUS <> CFG_BUS_X or CFG_MONR <> CFG_MONR_X or CFG_MONF <> CFG_MONF_X or CFG_MONF_NF <> CFG_MONF_NF_X
    rig_fail(string("CFG a configuration word differs from its decoded value"))
    ln_out()
  if CAP_4P <> CAP_4P_X or CAP_8P <> CAP_8P_X or CAP_16P <> CAP_16P_X
    rig_fail(string("CFG a streamer command word differs from its decoded value"))
    ln_out()
  if FILT0_ENG <> FILT0_ENG_X
    rig_fail(string("CFG the engagement HUBSET word differs from its decoded value"))
    ln_out()
  ln_s(string("WORDS (symbol composition = decoded value): BUS "))
  ln_h(CFG_BUS)
  ln_s(string(" MON_R "))
  ln_h(CFG_MONR)
  ln_s(string(" MON_F "))
  ln_h(CFG_MONF)
  ln_s(string(" MON_F unfiltered "))
  ln_h(CFG_MONF_NF)
  ln_s(string(" | capture 4P "))
  ln_h(CAP_4P)
  ln_s(string(" 8P "))
  ln_h(CAP_8P)
  ln_s(string(" 16P "))
  ln_h(CAP_16P)
  ln_s(string(" | engagement HUBSET "))
  ln_h(FILT0_ENG)
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' tables
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI mode_text(modeIdx) : pText
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @returns pText - the mode as printed

  pText := lookupz(modeIdx: string(" 4P"), string(" 8P"), string("16P"))

PRI rate_text(rateIdx) : pText
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @returns pText - the rung as printed

  pText := lookupz(rateIdx: string("1:16"), string("1:8 "), string("1:4 "), string("1:2 "), string("1:1 "))

PRI rate_nco(rateIdx) : ncoVal
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @returns ncoVal - the SETXFRQ value

  ncoVal := lookupz(rateIdx: NCO_1_16, NCO_1_8, NCO_1_4, NCO_1_2, NCO_1_1)

PRI rate_want(rateIdx) : wantVal
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @returns wantVal - samples between consecutive edges of the 64-clock stimulus

  wantVal := lookupz(rateIdx: FAST_PER / 16, FAST_PER / 8, FAST_PER / 4, FAST_PER / 2, FAST_PER)

PRI cap_word(modeIdx) : wordVal
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @returns wordVal - the streamer command word (count included)

  wordVal := lookupz(modeIdx: CAP_4P, CAP_8P, CAP_16P)

PRI cap_bytes(modeIdx) : byteCnt
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @returns byteCnt - bytes the capture must write for SAMPLES samples

  byteCnt := lookupz(modeIdx: SAMPLES / 2, SAMPLES, SAMPLES * 2)

PRI pat_val(patIdx) : patVal
' @param patIdx - gate A pattern 0..NPAT-1
' @returns patVal - the pattern driven on P32..P35 (bit 0 = P32)

  patVal := lookupz(patIdx: %0000, %0001, %1000, %0010, %0100, %0110)

PRI ln_pat(patVal)
' Append a pattern as %dddd (bit 3 = P35 first).
'
' @param patVal - the pattern

  ln_c("%")
  ln_c("0" + ((patVal >> 3) & 1))
  ln_c("0" + ((patVal >> 2) & 1))
  ln_c("0" + ((patVal >> 1) & 1))
  ln_c("0" + (patVal & 1))

PRI filt_text(filtIdx) : pText
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @returns pText - the leg as printed

  pText := lookupz(filtIdx: string("control, both monitors UNFILTERED"), string("ENGAGEMENT: filt0 = 5 flip-flops, tap 3 (about 40 clocks)"), string("filt0 = 2 flip-flops, tap 0"), string("filt0 = 3 flip-flops, tap 0"), string("filt0 = 5 flip-flops, tap 0"), string("filt0 = 8 flip-flops, tap 0"))

PRI filt_ff(filtIdx) : ffCnt
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @returns ffCnt - flip-flops of the leg's filter (0 for the control; the engagement leg is not read against this)

  ffCnt := lookupz(filtIdx: 0, 5, 2, 3, 5, 8)

PRI filt_word(filtIdx) : hubWord
' @param filtIdx - skew leg (not the control)
' @returns hubWord - the HUBSET word that configures filt0 for the leg
'                    (FILT0_BASE + length << 5 + tap; SD:2784)

  hubWord := lookupz(filtIdx: FILT0_BASE, FILT0_ENG, FILT0_BASE + (0 << 5), FILT0_BASE + (1 << 5), FILT0_BASE + (2 << 5), FILT0_BASE + (3 << 5))

' ===========================================================================
' THE MEASURING COG (Spin2).  Owns the streamer, the buffer and every pin.
' ===========================================================================
PRI worker() | modeIdx, filtIdx
' Run the gates and the two measurements; write DONE_V at the end.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local modeIdx - capture mode
' @local filtIdx - skew leg

  wPhase := PH_CERT
  certMask := certify_pins_free()
  if certMask <> 0
    wDone := DONE_V
    return
  wPhase := PH_A
  repeat modeIdx from MD_4P to MD_16P
    wDetail := modeIdx
    arm_a(modeIdx)
  wPhase := PH_O
  calibrate_order()
  wPhase := PH_C
  arm_c()
  wPhase := PH_D
  arm_d()
  wPhase := PH_E
  arm_e()
  wPhase := PH_S
  repeat filtIdx from SK_CTL to SK_FF8
    wDetail := filtIdx
    arm_s(filtIdx)
  hubset(FILT0_BASE)                    ' filt0 back to its default: length %00, tap 0 (SD:2808-2817)
  release_all()
  wPhase := PH_END
  wDone := DONE_V

PRI certify_pins_free() : busyMask
' Hold P32..P47 at a 15 kOhm LOW and read them back: anything attached
' overpowers 15 kOhm and reads 1.  Nothing is driven hard before this.
'
' @returns busyMask - bit n set when P(32+n) read 1 (0 = all free)

  pinclear(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)
  wrpin(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1, P_LOW_15K)
  pinlow(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)  ' DIR high, OUT low -> 15k to GIO
  waitms(1)
  busyMask := pinread(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)
  pinclear(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)

PRI release_all()
' Stop the streamer and return P32..P47 to reset.
'

  org
    xstop
  end
  pinclear(GUARD_LO addpins GUARD_N - 1)

PRI hold_weak()
' P36..P47 at a 15 kOhm low, so a wider capture reads 0 on lanes it does not use.
'

  wrpin(WEAK_LO addpins WEAK_N - 1, P_LOW_15K)
  pinlow(WEAK_LO addpins WEAK_N - 1)

PRI drive_pattern(nibVal) | i
' Drive P32..P35 hard to the levels in the low four bits of nibVal
' (bit 0 -> P32), plain pins, no smart mode, no routing.
'
' @param nibVal - the pattern

' Local Variables:
' @local i - pin index

  release_all()
  hold_weak()
  repeat i from 0 to 3
    pinclear(BUS + i)
    if nibVal & (1 << i)
      pinhigh(BUS + i)
    else
      pinlow(BUS + i)
  waitms(1)

PRI setup_stimulus(period, monfCfg)
' reset (DIRL) -> configure (WRPIN/WXPIN) -> enable (DIRH) -> operate (WYPIN).
' WYPIN comes after DIRH (EF-011: a WYPIN before enable is lost in the trigger
' modes, and TRANSITION is one of them).
'
' @param period - BUS base period in clocks
' @param monfCfg - the WRPIN word of MON_F (filtered or not)

  release_all()
  hold_weak()
  pinclear(BUS)
  wrpin(BUS, CFG_BUS)                   ' P_OE is required or the smart pin does not drive the pin
  wxpin(BUS, period)                    ' X[15:0] = base period in clocks
  pinlow(BUS)                           ' DIR high: enable; WYPIN (the start) comes after
  pinclear(MON_R)
  wrpin(MON_R, CFG_MONR)                ' DIR stays low: a monitor must not drive the net it watches
  pinclear(MON_F)
  wrpin(MON_F, monfCfg)
  pinclear(NULLPIN)
  pinlow(NULLPIN)                       ' the lane that must stay silent
  waitms(1)

PRI capture(modeIdx, xfrq, ycnt, shiftClk) : written, late | cmd, addr, budget, t0, t1
' One streamer capture into bufl: WRFAST, XINIT, the burst started right
' after (shiftClk clocks later when shiftClk is non-zero: gate O shifts the burst by
' whole samples to change the edge parity against the byte), a BOUNDED wait
' for the streamer to finish (a stalled streamer must not hang the cog), the
' FIFO drain, XSTOP.  The guard pad after bufl is refilled before and checked
' after every capture.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param xfrq - SETXFRQ value
' @param ycnt - transitions to start on BUS (0: none)
' @param shiftClk - clocks to wait between XINIT and the burst start (0: none)
' @returns written - bytes of bufl that are no longer the sentinel
' @returns late - 1 when the streamer did not signal XFI within the budget

' Local Variables:
' @local cmd - the streamer command word
' @local addr - hub address of the buffer
' @local budget - clocks allowed for the streamer to finish
' @local t0 - CT at XINIT
' @local t1 - CT in the wait loop

  bytefill(@bufl, SENTINEL, BUF_BYTES)
  longfill(@bufPad, PAD_FILL, PAD_LONGS)
  cmd := cap_word(modeIdx)
  addr := @bufl
  budget := CAP_BUDGET
  org
    setxfrq xfrq
    wrfast  #0, addr
    getct   t0
    xinit   cmd, #0
    tjz     shiftClk, #.noshiftClk        ' shiftClk = 0: no shift
    waitx   shiftClk
.noshiftClk
    wypin   ycnt, #BUS          ' starts the burst; harmless when ycnt = 0
.wait
    getct   t1
    sub     t1, t0
    cmp     t1, budget      wc
    if_nc   mov     late, #1        ' streamer never signalled XFI in budget
    if_nc   jmp     #.done
    pollxfi                 wc
    if_nc   jmp     #.wait
.done
    waitx   ##10_000
    xstop
  end
  written := bytes_written()
  capCount++
  if not pad_intact()
    padHits++

PRI pad_intact() : bIntact | i
' Whether the guard longs after bufl still hold PAD_FILL (the streamer did not
' write past the buffer).
'
' @returns bIntact - TRUE when no guard long changed

' Local Variables:
' @local i - guard long index

  bIntact := TRUE
  repeat i from 0 to PAD_LONGS - 1
    if long[@bufPad][i] <> PAD_FILL
      bIntact := FALSE

PRI bytes_written() : n | i
' How many bytes of the buffer are no longer the sentinel.
'
' @returns n - bytes written

' Local Variables:
' @local i - byte index

  repeat i from 0 to BUF_BYTES - 1
    if byte[@bufl][i] <> SENTINEL
      n++

PRI sample_val(modeIdx, n) : v
' Sample n of the capture: 4, 8 or 16 bits, bit 0 = the base pin P32.
' The 4-pin mode packs two samples per byte, the earlier one in the low
' nibble unless nibHi says otherwise (gate O).
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param n - sample index
' @returns v - the sample

  case modeIdx
    MD_4P:
      v := (byte[@bufl][n >> 1] >> (((n & 1) ^ nibHi) << 2)) & $F
    MD_8P:
      v := byte[@bufl][n]
    MD_16P:
      v := word[@bufl][n]

PRI count_not_equal(modeIdx, expectVal) : badCnt | n
' Samples (of the first SAMPLES) that differ from expectVal.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param expectVal - the required sample value
' @returns badCnt - samples that differ

' Local Variables:
' @local n - sample index

  repeat n from 0 to SAMPLES - 1
    if sample_val(modeIdx, n) <> expectVal
      badCnt++

PRI analyze(modeIdx, wantVal) | n, v, b, prevB, lastEdge, iv
' Statistics of the MON_R lane (edge count, first, last, shortest and longest
' interval between consecutive edges, intervals not equal to wantVal) and of
' the NULL lane (samples reading 1).  Results in the an* variables.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param wantVal - the required interval in samples

' Local Variables:
' @local n - sample index
' @local v - a sample
' @local b - the MON_R bit
' @local prevB - the previous MON_R bit (-1 before the first)
' @local lastEdge - sample index of the previous edge (-1 before the first)
' @local iv - interval between two consecutive edges

  anEdges := 0
  anFirst := -1
  anLast := -1
  anMin := POSX
  anMax := 0
  anBad := 0
  anNull := 0
  prevB := -1
  lastEdge := -1
  repeat n from 0 to SAMPLES - 1
    v := sample_val(modeIdx, n)
    anNull += (v >> LANE_NULL) & 1
    b := (v >> LANE_MONR) & 1
    if prevB <> -1 and b <> prevB
      anEdges++
      anLast := n
      if lastEdge >= 0
        iv := n - lastEdge
        anMin <#= iv
        anMax #>= iv
        if iv <> wantVal
          anBad++
      else
        anFirst := n
      lastEdge := n
    prevB := b

PRI is_exact(modeIdx, wrote, late, wantVal) : bExact
' Whether the analysed capture is EXACT: exactly the expected number of bytes
' written (fewer = dropped, more = over-run), no LATE, NULL lane silent,
' enough edges, every interval = wantVal.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param wrote - bytes written
' @param late - the LATE flag
' @param wantVal - the required interval
' @returns bExact - TRUE when exact

  bExact := wrote == cap_bytes(modeIdx) and late == 0 and anNull == 0 and anEdges >= MIN_EDGES and anBad == 0 and anMin == wantVal and anMax == wantVal

PRI lane_stats(modeIdx, lane) : edges, highs, first | n, b, prevB
' Edge count, samples high, and the index of the first edge of one lane.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param lane - lane (pin - P32)
' @returns edges - changes
' @returns highs - samples reading 1
' @returns first - index of the first change, or SAMPLES

' Local Variables:
' @local n - sample index
' @local b - the lane's bit
' @local prevB - the previous bit

  first := SAMPLES
  prevB := (sample_val(modeIdx, 0) >> lane) & 1
  highs := prevB
  repeat n from 1 to SAMPLES - 1
    b := (sample_val(modeIdx, n) >> lane) & 1
    highs += b
    if b <> prevB
      edges++
      if first == SAMPLES
        first := n
      prevB := b

PRI collect_edges(modeIdx, lane, pArr) : cnt | n, b, prevB
' The edges of one lane: each stored as (sample index << 1) | new level.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param lane - lane
' @param pArr - hub address of a long array of EDGE_MAX
' @returns cnt - edges stored (at most EDGE_MAX)

' Local Variables:
' @local n - sample index
' @local b - the lane's bit
' @local prevB - the previous bit (-1 before the first sample)

  prevB := -1
  repeat n from 0 to SAMPLES - 1
    b := (sample_val(modeIdx, n) >> lane) & 1
    if prevB <> -1 and b <> prevB and cnt < EDGE_MAX
      long[pArr][cnt] := (n << 1) | b
      cnt++
    prevB := b

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm A - the capture-path control, per mode
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_a(modeIdx) | k, nibVal, wrote, late, bad, baseIdx
' NPAT static captures per mode (patterns, bit 0 = P32: %0000, %0001, %1000,
' %0010, %0100, %0110).  A mode whose captures are not every-sample exact,
' write a different number of bytes than expected, or leave sentinel bytes,
' is VOID.  A2 and A3 drive opposite ends of the base group, A4 and A5 the two
' middle lanes (P33, P34) one at a time and A6 both together, so a lane
' mapping that swaps or merges any of the four lanes fails one of them by
' construction.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode

' Local Variables:
' @local k - A1..A6
' @local nibVal - the driven pattern
' @local wrote - bytes written
' @local late - the LATE flag
' @local bad - samples that differ from the pattern
' @local baseIdx - index of the record

  modeOk[modeIdx] := TRUE
  repeat k from 0 to NPAT - 1
    nibVal := pat_val(k)
    drive_pattern(nibVal)
    wrote, late := capture(modeIdx, NCO_1_4, 0, 0)
    bad := count_not_equal(modeIdx, nibVal)
    baseIdx := (modeIdx * NPAT + k) * AW
    aRec[baseIdx + AF_WROTE] := wrote
    aRec[baseIdx + AF_BAD] := bad
    aRec[baseIdx + AF_FIRST] := sample_val(modeIdx, 0)
    if wrote <> cap_bytes(modeIdx) or late <> 0 or bad <> 0
      modeOk[modeIdx] := FALSE
  release_all()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm O - 4-pin nibble order, measured at the slowest rung
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI calibrate_order() | tryIdx, wrote, late, exLo, exHi
' Capture the stimulus at 1:16 and analyse it BOTH low nibble first and high
' nibble first.  The order is decided only when exactly one analysis is exact.
' If both are exact the capture cannot tell the orders apart (every edge sits on
' a byte boundary), so the capture is repeated, the burst starting one 1:16
' sample (NIB_SHIFT clocks) later each try, up to NIB_TRIES times.  No try
' disagrees: nibState 3 (undetermined) and the 4-pin mode is VOID; neither
' analysis exact in any try that is not undetermined: nibState 2.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local tryIdx - capture number
' @local wrote - bytes written
' @local late - the LATE flag
' @local exLo - the capture is EXACT read low nibble first
' @local exHi - the capture is EXACT read high nibble first

  nibState := 2
  nibHi := 0
  nibTries := 0
  nibBoth := 0
  nibNeither := 0
  if not modeOk[MD_4P]
    return
  repeat tryIdx from 0 to NIB_TRIES - 1
    setup_stimulus(FAST_PER, CFG_MONF)
    wrote, late := capture(MD_4P, NCO_1_16, BURST_E, tryIdx * NIB_SHIFT)
    release_all()
    nibTries := tryIdx + 1
    nibHi := 0
    analyze(MD_4P, rate_want(RG_1_16))
    exLo := is_exact(MD_4P, wrote, late, rate_want(RG_1_16))
    nibHi := 1
    analyze(MD_4P, rate_want(RG_1_16))
    exHi := is_exact(MD_4P, wrote, late, rate_want(RG_1_16))
    if exLo and exHi
      nibBoth++
    elseif not exLo and not exHi
      nibNeither++
    else
      if exHi
        nibState := 1
      else
        nibState := 0
      nibHi := nibState
      quit
  if nibState == 2
    nibHi := 0
    if nibBoth > 0
      nibState := 3
    modeOk[MD_4P] := FALSE

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm C - the same contrast with NO STREAMER (the IN rule seen by the cog)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_c() | i, busCh, monCh, busPrev, monPrev, v
' While the BUS smart pin toggles, count the changes a plain cog read sees on
' P32 (its own IN = the completion flag) and on P33 (the routed neighbour =
' the pin level).  Count CHANGES, not levels: both signals sit high for about
' half the window.  The simplest layer answers first.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local i - read index
' @local busCh - changes seen on P32
' @local monCh - changes seen on P33
' @local busPrev - previous read of P32
' @local monPrev - previous read of P33
' @local v - one read

  setup_stimulus(SLOW_PER, CFG_MONF)
  wypin(BUS, BURST_C)                   ' a 12 ms burst of 300 us half-cycles
  busPrev := pinread(BUS)
  monPrev := pinread(MON_R)
  repeat i from 0 to C_SAMPLES - 1
    v := pinread(BUS)
    if v <> busPrev
      busCh++
      busPrev := v
    v := pinread(MON_R)
    if v <> monPrev
      monCh++
      monPrev := v
    waitus(C_INTERVAL)
  release_all()
  cBus := busCh
  cMon := monCh

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm D - both signals in ONE capture (the gate, and the skew carrier)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_d() | wrote, late, lane, edges, highs, first
' One 4-pin 1:1 capture of a 10-transition burst that ENDS INSIDE the window,
' so the BUS lane carries exactly one edge (the flag) if the IN rule holds.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local wrote - bytes written
' @local late - the LATE flag
' @local lane - lane
' @local edges - lane edges
' @local highs - lane samples high
' @local first - lane first edge

  setup_stimulus(FAST_PER, CFG_MONF)
  wrote, late := capture(MD_4P, NCO_1_1, BURST_D, 0)
  release_all()
  dRec[0] := wrote
  dRec[1] := late
  repeat lane from 0 to 3
    edges, highs, first := lane_stats(MD_4P, lane)
    dRec[2 + lane * 3] := edges
    dRec[3 + lane * 3] := highs
    dRec[4 + lane * 3] := first

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm E - the sustained-rate ladder
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_e() | modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx
' Every mode that passed gate A (and O), every rung, REPS repetitions.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local modeIdx - capture mode
' @local rateIdx - ladder rung
' @local repIdx - repetition

  repeat modeIdx from MD_4P to MD_16P
    if modeOk[modeIdx]
      repeat rateIdx from RG_1_16 to RG_1_1
        repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
          wDetail := (modeIdx << 8) + (rateIdx << 4) + repIdx
          one_rung(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx)

PRI one_rung(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx) | wrote, late, baseIdx, bExact
' One capture at one rung and its record.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @param repIdx - repetition

' Local Variables:
' @local wrote - bytes written
' @local late - the LATE flag
' @local baseIdx - index of the record
' @local bExact - the rung is EXACT

  setup_stimulus(FAST_PER, CFG_MONF)
  wrote, late := capture(modeIdx, rate_nco(rateIdx), BURST_E, 0)
  release_all()
  analyze(modeIdx, rate_want(rateIdx))
  bExact := is_exact(modeIdx, wrote, late, rate_want(rateIdx))
  baseIdx := ((modeIdx * NRATE + rateIdx) * REPS + repIdx) * EW
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_WROTE] := wrote
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_LATE] := late
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_EDGES] := anEdges
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_FIRST] := anFirst
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_LAST] := anLast
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_MIN] := anMin
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_MAX] := anMax
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_BAD] := anBad
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_NULL] := anNull
  eRec[baseIdx + EF_EXACT] := bExact & 1

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm S - filter skew at one sample per clock
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_s(filtIdx) | repIdx, wrote, late, monfCfg, cnA, cnB, i, n, d, baseIdx, rMin, rMax, fMin, fMax, nR, nF, dirMis
' One skew leg: SREPS captures of the 10-transition burst at 1:1 in the 4-pin
' mode; MON_R is always unfiltered, MON_F is unfiltered (the control leg) or
' filtered with filt0 set to the leg's length.  Per capture: the position of
' every MON_F edge minus the same-numbered MON_R edge, rising and falling.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local wrote - bytes written
' @local late - the LATE flag
' @local monfCfg - the WRPIN word of MON_F for this leg
' @local cnA - MON_R edges
' @local cnB - MON_F edges
' @local i - edge index
' @local n - edges compared
' @local d - MON_F position minus MON_R position
' @local baseIdx - index of the record
' @local rMin - least rising skew
' @local rMax - greatest rising skew
' @local fMin - least falling skew
' @local fMax - greatest falling skew
' @local nR - rising edges compared
' @local nF - falling edges compared
' @local dirMis - edge pairs whose directions differ

  if not modeOk[MD_4P]
    return
  if filtIdx == SK_CTL
    monfCfg := CFG_MONF_NF
  else
    monfCfg := CFG_MONF
    hubset(filt_word(filtIdx))          ' filt0: the engagement leg (5 flip-flops, tap 3) or length L (2, 3, 5, 8 flip-flops), tap 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to SREPS - 1
    setup_stimulus(FAST_PER, monfCfg)
    wrote, late := capture(MD_4P, NCO_1_1, BURST_D, 0)
    release_all()
    analyze(MD_4P, FAST_PER)           ' MON_R lane: every interval must be 64 samples at 1:1
    cnA := collect_edges(MD_4P, LANE_MONR, @tmpA)
    cnB := collect_edges(MD_4P, LANE_MONF, @tmpB)
    rMin := POSX
    rMax := NEGX
    fMin := POSX
    fMax := NEGX
    nR := 0
    nF := 0
    dirMis := 0
    n := cnA <# cnB
    if n > 0
      repeat i from 0 to n - 1
        if (tmpA[i] & 1) <> (tmpB[i] & 1)
          dirMis++
        else
          d := (tmpB[i] >> 1) - (tmpA[i] >> 1)
          if tmpA[i] & 1
            rMin <#= d
            rMax #>= d
            nR++
          else
            fMin <#= d
            fMax #>= d
            nF++
    baseIdx := (filtIdx * SREPS + repIdx) * SW
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_WROTE] := wrote
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_LATE] := late
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_BAD] := anBad
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_NULL] := anNull
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_NA] := cnA
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_NB] := cnB
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_DIRMIS] := dirMis
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_RMIN] := rMin
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_RMAX] := rMax
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_FMIN] := fMin
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_FMAX] := fMax
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_NR] := nR
    sRec[baseIdx + SF_NF] := nF
    if repIdx == 0
      longmove(@sEdgeA[filtIdx * EDGE_MAX], @tmpA, EDGE_MAX)
      longmove(@sEdgeB[filtIdx * EDGE_MAX], @tmpB, EDGE_MAX)
      sEdgeNA[filtIdx] := cnA
      sEdgeNB[filtIdx] := cnB

' ===========================================================================
' REPORTING (cog 0)
' ===========================================================================
PRI report_all() | modeIdx, filtIdx
' Print every record, the gate lines and the readings.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local modeIdx - capture mode
' @local filtIdx - skew leg

  if wPhase < PH_CERT
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the measuring cog never started a phase - NO VERDICT"))
    failCnt++
  if certMask <> 0
    ln_s(string("STOP: P32..P47 are not free - pins reading 1 under the weak low, mask (bit 0 = P32) "))
    ln_h(certMask)
    ln_out()
    say(string("   Nothing was driven hard. Detach whatever is on those pins and run again."))
    say(string("=== END: PINS BUSY - NO VERDICT ==="))
    return
  say(string("CERT passed: P32..P47 all read 0 under the 15k low"))
  say(string("--- GATE A: static captures per mode (A1 %0000, A2 %0001, A3 %1000, A4 %0010, A5 %0100, A6 %0110; bit 0 = P32); bad = samples differing from the pattern ---"))
  repeat modeIdx from MD_4P to MD_16P
    report_a(modeIdx)
  report_o()
  report_c()
  report_d()
  say(string("--- ARM E: sustained capture rate (stimulus toggles every 64 clocks; rung EXACT = every interval = 64/N) ---"))
  repeat modeIdx from MD_4P to MD_16P
    report_e(modeIdx)
  say(string("--- ARM S: filter skew (MON_F edge position minus MON_R edge position, clocks; positive = MON_F later) ---"))
  repeat filtIdx from SK_CTL to SK_FF8
    report_s(filtIdx)
  report_s_verdict()
  ln_s(string("PAD: the "))
  ln_d(PAD_LONGS)
  ln_s(string(" guard longs after the buffer were changed in "))
  ln_cnt(padHits, capCount)
  ln_s(string(" captures (0 = no over-run)"))
  ln_out()
  if padHits <> 0
    rig_fail(string("PAD the streamer wrote past the end of the capture buffer - the capture buffer is overrun, the captures are not trustworthy"))
    ln_out()
  ln_s(string("=== GATES: "))
  if failCnt == 0
    say(string("all passed ==="))
  else
    ln_d(failCnt)
    say(string(" RIG FAIL line(s) above - the results they cover are withheld, the raw values stand ==="))
  say(string("=== END ==="))

PRI report_a(modeIdx) | k, baseIdx
' Gate A for one mode.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode

' Local Variables:
' @local k - A1..A6
' @local baseIdx - index of the record

  repeat k from 0 to NPAT - 1
    baseIdx := (modeIdx * NPAT + k) * AW
    ln_s(string("A"))
    ln_d(k + 1)
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_pat(pat_val(k))
    ln_s(string(": bytes written "))
    ln_d(aRec[baseIdx + AF_WROTE])
    ln_s(string(" (need exactly "))
    ln_d(cap_bytes(modeIdx))
    ln_s(string("), samples differing from the pattern "))
    ln_d(aRec[baseIdx + AF_BAD])
    ln_s(string(", sample 0 = "))
    ln_h(aRec[baseIdx + AF_FIRST])
    ln_out()
  if modeOk[modeIdx]
    ln_s(string("A PASSED "))
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    say(string(": the path writes, discriminates, and lane N = pin P(32+N)"))
  else
    rig_fail(string("A "))
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    ln_s(string(" - a static capture was not exact (or the order gate O failed): this mode is VOID, no ladder is run for it"))
    ln_out()

PRI report_o()
' Gate O.
'

  ln_s(string("O: "))
  ln_d(nibTries)
  ln_s(string(" capture(s) at 1:16 (burst start shifted 16 clocks per try); tries where both orders were exact "))
  ln_d(nibBoth)
  ln_s(string(", neither "))
  ln_d(nibNeither)
  ln_out()
  case nibState
    0:
      say(string("O PASSED: 4-pin samples are packed LOW nibble first (SD:1456 'bits bottom-first'); in the deciding capture low-first was exact and high-first was NOT"))
    1:
      say(string("O PASSED (finding): 4-pin samples are packed HIGH nibble first - the opposite of the low-nibble-first reading; in the deciding capture high-first was exact and low-first was NOT"))
    3:
      rig_fail(string("O nibble order undetermined: low-first and high-first were both exact in every usable try, so the capture cannot tell the orders apart - the 4-pin mode is VOID, no ladder or skew verdict"))
      ln_out()
    other:
      if modeOk[MD_4P] == 0
        rig_fail(string("O the 4-pin 1:16 capture was exact in NEITHER nibble order (or gate A failed first): the 4-pin mode is VOID"))
        ln_out()

PRI report_c()
' Arm C: the IN contrast with no streamer.
'

  ln_s(string("C (no streamer, 20 ms, 300 us half-cycles, 50 us reads): P32 (BUS, its own IN) changes "))
  ln_d(cBus)
  ln_s(string(" | P33 (MON_R, the routed neighbour) changes "))
  ln_d(cMon)
  ln_out()
  if cMon == UNWRITTEN
    rig_fail(string("C was not run"))
    ln_out()
  elseif cMon < 20
    rig_fail(string("C the stimulus did not run - P33 never tracked the wire; arm D and the ladder are not interpretable"))
    ln_out()
  elseif cBus <= 2
    say(string("C as the documented IN rule says: the routed neighbour tracked the wire; the smart pin's own IN changed once (the completion flag)"))
  elseif cBus >= 20
    say(string("C FINDING: P32's own IN tracked the waveform too - the IN rule does not hold for this mode (the stimulus is alive)"))
  else
    say(string("C FINDING: P32's change count falls between the flag (<= 2) and the waveform (>= 20); the two counts above are the record"))

PRI report_d() | lane
' Arm D: the headline contrast in one capture, and the NULL-lane gate.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local lane - lane

  if dRec[0] == UNWRITTEN
    rig_fail(string("D was not run"))
    ln_out()
    return
  ln_s(string("D (4-pin, 1:1, 10-transition burst): bytes "))
  ln_d(dRec[0])
  ln_s(string(", late "))
  ln_d(dRec[1])
  ln_out()
  repeat lane from 0 to 3
    ln_s(string("   lane "))
    ln_d(lane)
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(lookupz(lane: string("P32 BUS  smart pin "), string("P33 MON_R routed   "), string("P34 MON_F routed   "), string("P35 NULL  control  ")))
    ln_s(string(": edges "))
    ln_d(dRec[2 + lane * 3])
    ln_s(string(" highs "))
    ln_d(dRec[3 + lane * 3])
    ln_s(string(" first edge at "))
    ln_d(dRec[4 + lane * 3])
    ln_out()
  if dRec[2 + LANE_NULL * 3] <> 0 or dRec[3 + LANE_NULL * 3] <> 0
    rig_fail(string("D the NULL lane (P35, driven low) carries data - the lane mapping is wrong for this capture"))
    ln_out()
  elseif dRec[2 + LANE_MONR * 3] < MIN_EDGES
    rig_fail(string("D the MON_R lane is flat - the stimulus did not run in this capture"))
    ln_out()
  elseif dRec[2 + LANE_BUS * 3] <= 1
    say(string("D as the documented IN rule says: the BUS lane carries at most one edge (the flag) while the routed lane carries the waveform"))
  elseif dRec[2 + LANE_BUS * 3] >= MIN_EDGES
    say(string("D FINDING: the BUS lane carries the WAVEFORM too - the IN rule does not hold in a capture either"))
  else
    say(string("D FINDING: the BUS lane edge count is between the flag and the waveform; the counts above are the record"))

PRI rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : fieldVal
' One field of one ladder record.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - EF_*
' @returns fieldVal - the recorded long

  fieldVal := eRec[((modeIdx * NRATE + rateIdx) * REPS + repIdx) * EW + fieldIdx]

PRI exact_cnt(modeIdx, rateIdx) : cnt | repIdx
' Repetitions of one rung that were EXACT.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode
' @param rateIdx - ladder rung
' @returns cnt - exact repetitions

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition

  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    if rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_EXACT) == 1
      cnt++

PRI report_e(modeIdx) | rateIdx, repIdx, ceilIdx, bMono, bStopped
' One mode's ladder: a line per rung, the raw records of a rung that is not
' exact, then the reading.
'
' @param modeIdx - capture mode

' Local Variables:
' @local rateIdx - ladder rung
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local ceilIdx - the fastest rung exact with every slower rung exact (-1: none)
' @local bMono - no faster rung is exact above a failing one
' @local bStopped - a failing rung has been seen

  if not modeOk[modeIdx]
    ln_s(string("E "))
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    say(string(": VOID - gate A (or O) failed; no ladder was run"))
    return
  ceilIdx := -1
  bMono := TRUE
  bStopped := FALSE
  repeat rateIdx from RG_1_16 to RG_1_1
    ln_s(string("E "))
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(rate_text(rateIdx))
    ln_s(string(" want "))
    ln_d(rate_want(rateIdx))
    ln_s(string(": EXACT "))
    ln_cnt(exact_cnt(modeIdx, rateIdx), REPS)
    ln_s(string(" | rep 0: bytes "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_WROTE))
    ln_s(string("/"))
    ln_d(cap_bytes(modeIdx))
    ln_s(string(" late "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_LATE))
    ln_s(string(" edges "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_EDGES))
    ln_s(string(" interval "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_MIN))
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_MAX))
    ln_s(string(" bad "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_BAD))
    ln_s(string(" null "))
    ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, 0, EF_NULL))
    ln_out()
    if exact_cnt(modeIdx, rateIdx) <> REPS
      repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
        ln_s(string("      raw rep "))
        ln_d(repIdx)
        ln_s(string(": exact "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_EXACT))
        ln_s(string(" bytes "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_WROTE))
        ln_s(string(" late "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_LATE))
        ln_s(string(" edges "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_EDGES))
        ln_s(string(" first/last edge "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_FIRST))
        ln_s(string("/"))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_LAST))
        ln_s(string(" interval "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_MIN))
        ln_s(string(".."))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_MAX))
        ln_s(string(" bad "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_BAD))
        ln_s(string(" null "))
        ln_d(rec_e(modeIdx, rateIdx, repIdx, EF_NULL))
        ln_out()
    if exact_cnt(modeIdx, rateIdx) == REPS
      if bStopped
        bMono := FALSE
      else
        ceilIdx := rateIdx
    else
      bStopped := TRUE
  ' ---- gate E0 and the reading ----
  if exact_cnt(modeIdx, RG_1_16) <> REPS
    rig_fail(string("E0 "))
    ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
    ln_s(string(" the 1:16 rung is not exact in every repetition - this mode has no ceiling reading (the stimulus or the analysis, not the rate)"))
    ln_out()
    return
  ln_s(string("E READING "))
  ln_s(mode_text(modeIdx))
  ln_s(string(": "))
  if not bMono
    say(string("NON-MONOTONE - a faster rung is exact above a failing rung; the lines above are the finding"))
  elseif ceilIdx == RG_1_1
    say(string("NO CEILING REACHED - every rung 1:16 .. 1:1 EXACT in every repetition: this mode sustained one sample per clock with this stimulus"))
  else
    ln_s(string("CEILING "))
    ln_s(rate_text(ceilIdx))
    ln_s(string(" - the fastest exact rung; the first failing rung is "))
    ln_s(rate_text(ceilIdx + 1))
    say(string(" (its raw records above are the failure mode)"))

PRI rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : fieldVal
' One field of one skew record.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - SF_*
' @returns fieldVal - the recorded long

  fieldVal := sRec[(filtIdx * SREPS + repIdx) * SW + fieldIdx]

PRI skew_stat(filtIdx, bRise, bMax) : valVal | repIdx, v
' The least (bMax = FALSE) or greatest (TRUE) rising or falling skew over
' the repetitions.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @param bRise - TRUE: rising edges, FALSE: falling
' @param bMax - TRUE: the greatest, FALSE: the least
' @returns valVal - the skew in clocks (POSX / NEGX when no edge was compared)

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local v - one repetition's value

  if bMax
    valVal := NEGX
  else
    valVal := POSX
  repeat repIdx from 0 to SREPS - 1
    if bRise and bMax
      v := rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_RMAX)
    elseif bRise
      v := rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_RMIN)
    elseif bMax
      v := rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_FMAX)
    else
      v := rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_FMIN)
    if bMax
      valVal #>= v
    else
      valVal <#= v

PRI carrier_ok(filtIdx) : bOk | repIdx
' Gate S0 for one leg: in every repetition the MON_R lane is exact (bad = 0),
' the NULL lane silent, every capture written and not late, both monitors saw
' MIN_EDGES or more edges and the same number of them.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @returns bOk - TRUE when every repetition is a usable carrier

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition

  bOk := modeOk[MD_4P]
  repeat repIdx from 0 to SREPS - 1
    if rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_BAD) <> 0 or rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NULL) <> 0 or rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_LATE) <> 0
      bOk := FALSE
    if rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_WROTE) <> cap_bytes(MD_4P) or rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NA) < MIN_EDGES
      bOk := FALSE
    if rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NA) <> rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NB) or rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_DIRMIS) <> 0
      bOk := FALSE

PRI report_s(filtIdx) | repIdx, k, nA, nB
' One skew leg: the per-repetition records, then rep 0's edge positions.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local k - edge index
' @local nA - MON_R edges stored
' @local nB - MON_F edges stored

  ln_s(string("S "))
  ln_s(filt_text(filtIdx))
  ln_out()
  if not modeOk[MD_4P]
    say(string("   VOID - the 4-pin mode failed gate A or O"))
    return
  repeat repIdx from 0 to SREPS - 1
    ln_s(string("   rep "))
    ln_d(repIdx)
    ln_s(string(": MON_R edges "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NA))
    ln_s(string(" MON_F edges "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NB))
    ln_s(string(" direction mismatches "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_DIRMIS))
    ln_s(string(" | rising skew "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_RMIN))
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_RMAX))
    ln_s(string(" (n "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NR))
    ln_s(string(") falling skew "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_FMIN))
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_FMAX))
    ln_s(string(" (n "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NF))
    ln_s(string(") | MON_R intervals not 64: "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_BAD))
    ln_s(string(" NULL highs "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_NULL))
    ln_s(string(" late "))
    ln_d(rec_s(filtIdx, repIdx, SF_LATE))
    ln_out()
  nA := sEdgeNA[filtIdx]
  nB := sEdgeNB[filtIdx]
  ln_s(string("   rep 0 edge positions (sample << 1 | new level), MON_R:"))
  if nA > 0
    repeat k from 0 to nA - 1
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_d(sEdgeA[filtIdx * EDGE_MAX + k])
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("   rep 0 edge positions, MON_F:"))
  if nB > 0
    repeat k from 0 to nB - 1
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_d(sEdgeB[filtIdx * EDGE_MAX + k])
  ln_out()
  if not carrier_ok(filtIdx)
    rig_fail(string("S0 "))
    ln_s(filt_text(filtIdx))
    ln_s(string(": a capture was not a usable carrier (MON_R intervals not exact, NULL lane active, LATE, too few edges, edge counts or directions differ) - this leg's skew is withheld"))
    ln_out()

PRI eng_observed() : bEngaged | repIdx
' Whether the ENGAGEMENT leg showed the filter: the carrier gate S0 passed and,
' in every repetition, both edge directions were compared and every skew lies
' in ENG_MIN..ENG_MAX clocks.
'
' @returns bEngaged - TRUE when the filter was observed to engage

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition

  bEngaged := modeOk[MD_4P] and carrier_ok(SK_ENG)
  repeat repIdx from 0 to SREPS - 1
    if rec_s(SK_ENG, repIdx, SF_NR) == 0 or rec_s(SK_ENG, repIdx, SF_NF) == 0
      bEngaged := FALSE
  if skew_stat(SK_ENG, TRUE, FALSE) < ENG_MIN or skew_stat(SK_ENG, FALSE, FALSE) < ENG_MIN
    bEngaged := FALSE
  if skew_stat(SK_ENG, TRUE, TRUE) > ENG_MAX or skew_stat(SK_ENG, FALSE, TRUE) > ENG_MAX
    bEngaged := FALSE

PRI skew_reading(filtIdx, bRise, bEngaged) : pText | lo, hi, ff
' The pre-registered reading of one edge direction of one leg.  A 0 skew is
' NO DELAY only when the engagement leg showed that the filter reaches the
' captured lane; otherwise it is void.
'
' @param filtIdx - skew leg
' @param bRise - TRUE: rising edges
' @param bEngaged - the filter was observed to engage (the control leg ignores it)
' @returns pText - the reading as text

' Local Variables:
' @local lo - least skew over the repetitions
' @local hi - greatest skew over the repetitions
' @local ff - flip-flops of the filter

  lo := skew_stat(filtIdx, bRise, FALSE)
  hi := skew_stat(filtIdx, bRise, TRUE)
  ff := filt_ff(filtIdx)
  if lo == POSX
    pText := string("no edge compared")
  elseif lo <> hi
    pText := string("OTHER - the skew varies between edges or repetitions")
  elseif lo == 0 and filtIdx <> SK_CTL and not bEngaged
    pText := string("0 clocks (NO DELAY is VOID: filter not observed to engage)")
  elseif lo == 0
    pText := string("NO DELAY (0 clocks)")
  elseif ff > 0 and lo == ff
    pText := string("EQUALS N-FF (skew = the flip-flop count)")
  elseif ff > 0 and lo == ff - 1
    pText := string("EQUALS N-FF - 1")
  else
    pText := string("OTHER - a constant that is neither 0, N-FF nor N-FF - 1")

PRI report_s_verdict() | filtIdx, bEngaged
' Print the engagement reading, then the skew readings of the legs whose
' carrier gate passed.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local filtIdx - skew leg
' @local bEngaged - the engagement leg showed the filter

  say(string("--- S READINGS (a leg whose gate S0 failed is withheld) ---"))
  bEngaged := eng_observed()
  ln_s(string("S ENGAGEMENT "))
  ln_s(filt_text(SK_ENG))
  if modeOk[MD_4P] and carrier_ok(SK_ENG)
    ln_s(string(": rising ["))
    ln_d(skew_stat(SK_ENG, TRUE, FALSE))
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(skew_stat(SK_ENG, TRUE, TRUE))
    ln_s(string("] falling ["))
    ln_d(skew_stat(SK_ENG, FALSE, FALSE))
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(skew_stat(SK_ENG, FALSE, TRUE))
    ln_s(string("] clocks (ENGAGED needs every skew in "))
    ln_d(ENG_MIN)
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(ENG_MAX)
    ln_s(string("): "))
  else
    ln_s(string(": withheld (4-pin mode void or gate S0 failed): "))
  if bEngaged
    say(string("ENGAGED - the captured lane follows the filtered pin; the tap-0 legs below are valid readings"))
  else
    say(string("filter not observed to engage; NO DELAY is void (a 0 skew below says nothing about the filter)"))
  repeat filtIdx from SK_CTL to SK_FF8
    if filtIdx <> SK_ENG and modeOk[MD_4P] and carrier_ok(filtIdx)
      ln_s(string("S READING "))
      ln_s(filt_text(filtIdx))
      ln_s(string(": rising ["))
      ln_d(skew_stat(filtIdx, TRUE, FALSE))
      ln_s(string(".."))
      ln_d(skew_stat(filtIdx, TRUE, TRUE))
      ln_s(string("] "))
      ln_s(skew_reading(filtIdx, TRUE, bEngaged))
      ln_s(string(" | falling ["))
      ln_d(skew_stat(filtIdx, FALSE, FALSE))
      ln_s(string(".."))
      ln_d(skew_stat(filtIdx, FALSE, TRUE))
      ln_s(string("] "))
      ln_s(skew_reading(filtIdx, FALSE, bEngaged))
      if filtIdx <> SK_CTL and not bEngaged
        ln_s(string(" | filter not observed to engage; NO DELAY is void"))
      ln_out()
  if modeOk[MD_4P] and carrier_ok(SK_CTL) and (skew_stat(SK_CTL, TRUE, FALSE) <> 0 or skew_stat(SK_CTL, TRUE, TRUE) <> 0 or skew_stat(SK_CTL, FALSE, FALSE) <> 0 or skew_stat(SK_CTL, FALSE, TRUE) <> 0)
    rig_fail(string("S the control (two UNFILTERED monitors) is not 0: the capture path itself skews lanes, the filter skew is not separable from it"))
    ln_out()

